  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> be independent events such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>. The largest value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>, for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> (exactly one of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> occurs)<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>, is:"
  },
